1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,175
In an earlier video, The Thought Provocateur told viewers, "technically these heat
pump tax credits based on the bill that was signed are available through 2033".

2
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:19,663
The credit was real while it lasted: 30 percent of the cost
of a qualifying heat pump, capped at $2,000 a year from 2023.

3
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:33,054
But it was cut short: the IRS says it is not allowed for any property placed in service after
December 31, 2025; a qualifying heat pump in service before that deadline can still claim it.

4
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:44,704
And what ended is federal: the IRS lists it by code section, 25C
beside 25D; state and utility rebates are separate programmes.

5
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:49,846
What a heat pump really costs is the
question the full inquiry takes on.
